WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.009 --> 00:00:03.759
(majestic music)

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:11.800
- [Narrator] For thousands
of years the Dukha people

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.910
have lived in the
northernmost part of Mongolia

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.183
where breeding reindeer is a way of life.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:21.230
Today, they're the last
nomadic reindeer herders

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:22.063
in the world.

00:00:47.976 --> 00:00:50.559
(upbeat music)

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:13.880
- [Narrator] In Mongolian folklore,

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:17.240
reindeer are mystical creatures
believed to carry the spirit

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.110
of past loved ones.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:22.413
But most Mongolians have never
come face to face with one.

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:25.420
The animals prefer a region most people

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:27.133
would find uninhabitable.

00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:51.500
- [Narrator] Despite the harsh conditions,

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.580
these herders mainly rely
on their reindeer for milk

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:57.653
and transport and take
pride in raising them.

